sec.p:
S. mutans (ATCC25175) was obtained from Iranian Research Organization of Science and Technology (IROST) in lyophilized form. The bacterial powder was diluted with physiological serum and then cultured in BHI medium supplemented with 5% sheep blood. Petri dishes were incubated for 48 h at 37 °C and then colonies were sampled and placed in BHIB medium for 2 h at 37 °C. Then, the sterile tube containing the bacterial suspension was placed in a spectrophotometer and the optical density (OD) was read at 600 nm. The OD of the suspension in values of 0.08 to 0.11 was considered equivalent to the standard half-McFarland turbidity (1.5 \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
